.el .ds Aq '
.TH delete 1  "delete " 
.SH NAME
delete \- Remove sessions from the remote (the local file stays)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdelete\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISESSIONS\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove the remote copy of a session and its index entry.
.PP
The local file is never touched.
.PP
EXAMPLE:
    agr sync delete claude/a.cast.gz
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would happen, change nothing
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
List every session, not only the summary
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISESSIONS\fR>
Sessions to delete from the remote
